   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let p(x) = ln(x + 2) / (x^2 - 7x + 10). Consider the largest interval that contains x = 0 and on which p is continuous. How many integers does that interval contain?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 3
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The logarithm requires x + 2 > 0, so x > -2, and the denominator (x - 2)(x - 5) is zero at x = 2 and x = 5.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               2
            ],
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               5
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "p is a quotient of a logarithmic function and a polynomial, each continuous on its domain, so p is continuous on its domain (-2, 2) U (2, 5) U (5, infinity).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            "x",
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The piece containing x = 0 is (-2, 2), open at -2 because ln is undefined at 0 and open at 2 because the denominator vanishes.",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The integers in (-2, 2) are -1, 0 and 1.",
         "mathjson": 3
      }
   ],
